     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically given as 850 mg three times daily. The risk is serious, mainly lactic acidosis, and it applies even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
